<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/documents-review.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/documents-review-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/documents-review.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Appraisal process</span></nav><p class="kicker">Process guide</p><h1>How Insurance Appraisal Works in Indiana</h1><p class="lede">Seven stages from the first disagreement to a signed award: what happens, who does what and where Indiana claims most often go wrong.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line" href="/contact-us/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Stages</dt><dd>7</dd></div><div><dt>Panel</dt><dd>2 appraisers + umpire</dd></div><div><dt>Binding</dt><dd>2 of 3 signatures</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<p>Indiana does not have a statute that writes the appraisal process for homeowners and commercial property policies. Your rights come from the appraisal condition in your own policy, read together with Indiana contract law. The wording varies by carrier, so treat this guide as a map of how appraisal commonly runs, then check each step against your policy.</p>
<h2>1. Confirm it is an amount dispute</h2><p>Appraisal resolves how much a covered loss costs. Before anything else, confirm the carrier has accepted coverage for at least part of the loss and that the disagreement is about scope or price, not whether the policy applies.</p><h2>2. Read the clause and the calendar</h2><p>Find the appraisal condition in your policy, note how long each side has to name an appraiser, and calendar the suit-limitation date. Appraisal may not stop that clock.</p><h2>3. Send the written demand</h2><p>Either side can demand appraisal in writing. The demand identifies the claim, states that the parties disagree on the amount of loss and names your appraiser or commits to naming one within the policy window.</p><h2>4. Both appraisers inspect and estimate</h2><p>Each appraiser inspects the property and builds or refines a line-item estimate. Good appraisers document measurements, photos and pricing sources for every disputed line.</p><h2>5. Appraisers negotiate line by line</h2><p>The two appraisers compare estimates item by item. Many disputes narrow sharply here, and an agreed award signed by both appraisers ends the process.</p><h2>6. The umpire decides what is left</h2><p>Items the appraisers can’t agree on go to the umpire they selected, or one appointed by a court if they couldn’t agree. The umpire reviews submissions, may inspect, and decides each item.</p><h2>7. Sign the award and get paid</h2><p>An award signed by any two of the three panel members sets the amount of loss. The carrier then applies the deductible, depreciation and limits and issues payment under the policy.</p>
<h2>How long it takes</h2>
<p>A residential file with a clear scope often wraps up in two to three months after both appraisers are named. Large commercial losses, contents-heavy claims and files that need an umpire hearing can take longer. Delays most often come from incomplete documentation, so the work you do before the demand pays off later.</p>
<h2>What it costs</h2>
<p>Each side pays its own appraiser, and most policies split the umpire’s fee equally. Appraiser fees may be a flat amount, hourly or a percentage of the increase. Get the arrangement in writing before anyone starts, and run your numbers through the <a href="/claim-gap-tools/claim-gap-net-recovery-estimator/">claim gap and net recovery estimator</a>.</p>
<h2>Where appraisal stops</h2>
<p>An appraisal panel values the loss. It doesn’t decide coverage, interpret disputed policy language beyond what valuation requires, or award damages for bad faith. Indiana courts recognize that insurers owe policyholders a duty of good faith and fair dealing, and the state’s unfair claim settlement practices law is enforced by the Indiana Department of Insurance. Whether a particular claim was mishandled is a legal question for an Indiana attorney.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Before you demand</b>Run through the <a href="/claim-gap-tools/appraisal-readiness-checkup/">appraisal readiness checkup</a>. A complete file is the single biggest factor in a good award.</div>
</article><aside class="sidebar"><div class="sticky"><div class="side-box call-box"><p class="side-h">Talk it through</p><p>A free first conversation. We’ll tell you honestly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="call-num" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-gold btn-block" href="/contact-us/">Send claim details</a></div><div class="side-box"><p class="side-h">Resources</p><ul class="side-list"><li><a href="/appraisal-process-indiana/" aria-current="page">Appraisal process guide</a></li><li><a href="/indiana-appraisal-questions/">Appraisal FAQ</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-appraisal-terms/">Appraisal glossary</a></li><li><a href="/claim-dispute-guides/">Claim dispute guides</a></li></ul></div></div></aside></div><section class="cta-band"><div class="checker thin" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="wrap cta-in rv"><div><h2>Is the carrier’s number short?</h2><p>Send us the estimate. We’ll read it line by line and tell you what we see.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/contact-us/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
